WEBVTT

00:00:00.423 --> 00:00:04.633
How do you find your way from the whole
upper secondary physics curriculum

00:00:04.743 --> 00:00:06.673
down to a single experiment?

00:00:06.993 --> 00:00:09.223
Let's explore the advanced physics course

00:00:09.243 --> 00:00:12.785
on the nine-year school track
in the German state of Hesse.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.310
My Learning Goals shows
both stages of secondary school.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.544
Double-click on Upper Secondary
to open it.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.220
Here are the introductory phase

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.280
and the four semesters
of the qualification phase.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.975
Let's open the introductory phase.

00:00:30.227 --> 00:00:33.327
We want to see how motion is described.

00:00:33.677 --> 00:00:35.577
Let's open the first topic,

00:00:35.777 --> 00:00:38.988
then choose Free Fall of Heavy Balls.

00:00:39.293 --> 00:00:41.403
Here's what you'll learn in this unit.

00:00:42.113 --> 00:00:44.913
Start on the left with a falling ball.

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:49.592
Then log the drop height and fall time
in your lab notes.

00:00:50.023 --> 00:00:51.863
Follow the arrows to the right.

00:00:52.183 --> 00:00:54.443
The graph leads to acceleration,

00:00:54.643 --> 00:00:56.963
and then to measurement uncertainty.

00:00:57.433 --> 00:01:00.533
Next, investigate free fall experimentally.

00:01:00.853 --> 00:01:02.693
Here it all comes together.

00:01:03.013 --> 00:01:06.405
Use your measurements to find
the acceleration due to gravity.
